@api = http://localhost:3000/api/auth
# Define testPassword in a local REST Client environment before running requests.

### 1. Registro correcto
POST {{api}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Peter Parker",
  "email": "peter@dailybugle.com",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### 2. Registro con correo duplicado (espera 409)
POST {{api}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Otro Peter",
  "email": "peter@dailybugle.com",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### 3. Registro con datos inválidos (espera 400)
POST {{api}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "P",
  "email": "no-es-correo",
  "password": "123"
}

### 4. Registro intentando ser admin (espera 400, campo no permitido)
POST {{api}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Hacker",
  "email": "hacker@test.com",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}",
  "role": "admin"
}

### 5. Login correcto (copia el token de la respuesta)
# @name login
POST {{api}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "peter@dailybugle.com",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### 6. Login con contraseña incorrecta (espera 401)
POST {{api}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "peter@dailybugle.com",
  "password": "incorrecta123"
}

### 7. Perfil con token (espera 200)
GET {{api}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 8. Perfil sin token (espera 401)
GET {{api}}/me